          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The classical
            %em Brown representability theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Brown62"}> Brown 62
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Adams71"} Adams 71
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            on the (pointed)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            satisfying two conditions (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+functors"}> Brown functors
            ”) are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
          %p
            This is used notably to show that every additive reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
            is representable by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^n(X) \simeq [X,E_n]
                  \\,.
          %p
            (But beware that the cohomology theory in general contains less information than the spectrum, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phantom+maps"} phantom maps
            (see also this
            = succeed ").)" do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/117684/381"} MO discussion
          %p
            The Brown representability theorem as such, with the two conditions on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+functor"} Brown functor
            understood, only applies to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functors"} contravariant functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spanier-Whitehead+duality"} Spanier-Whitehead duality
            it implies at least over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complexes"} finite CW-complexes
            that dually every additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
            is representable by a spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            via
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_n(X) \simeq \pi_n(E_n \wedge X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            There are various generalizations, such as to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Neeman96"}> Neeman 96
            ), to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories of
            various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jardine09"}> Jardine 09
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#LurieHigherAlgebra"}> Lurie, theorem 1.4.1.2
            ). But in any case there are some crucial conditions for the theorem to apply, such as
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              structure on the values of the functor, as is the case for an (abelian) cohomology theory, and as would be the case for a represented functor in any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
          %p OR
          %ul
            %li
              the existence of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+generator"} strong generator
              in the homotopy category in question.
          %p
            In particular, there is no Brown representability theorem for functors from the homotopy category of pointed not-necessarily-connected spaces to pointed sets, or for functors from the homotopy category of unpointed spaces to sets. In fact, there are counterexamples in these two cases (
            %a{:href => "#FreydHeller93"}> Freyd-Heller 93
            , see remark
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Counterexamples"}
          %h2#ClassicalFormulation Classical formulation for homotopy functors on topological spaces
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top_*^c)
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            — or equivalently the homotopy category of pointed connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mo *
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top_*^c)
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            (given by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sums"} wedge sums
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} weak pushouts
            (namely,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushouts"} homotopy pushouts
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "weak+limit#RelationToHomotopyLimits"} weak limit
          #ClassicalBrownRepresentabilityTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Brown-Adams)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mo *
                      %mi c
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:Ho(Top_*^c)^{op} \to Set_*
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              precisely if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} takes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              %li
                %p
                  it takes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pushouts"} weak pushouts
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pullbacks"} weak pullbacks
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrito02"} Aguilar-Gitler-Prito 02, theorem 12.2.18
          %p Note that it is immediate that every representable functor has the given properties; the nontrivial statement is that these properties already characterize representable functors.
          %p
            When the theorem is stated in terms of CW complexes, the second property (taking
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pushouts"} weak pushouts
            to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pullbacks"} weak pullbacks
          %ul
            %li
              The
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong Mayer-Vietoris axiom
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-pair"} CW-triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ;
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X; A_1, A_2)
              (with
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1\cup A_2 = X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1\in F(A_1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2\in F(A_2)
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1|A_1\cap A_2 = x_2|A_1\cap A_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in F(X)
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y|A_1 = x_1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y|A_2 = x_2
          #Counterexamples.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong (counterexamples)
            %p
              The statement of theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalBrownRepresentabilityTheorem"}
              without the restriction to
              %em connected
              pointed spaces is false, as is the analogous statement for unpointed spaces.
            %p
              In (
              %a{:href => "#FreydHeller93"}> Freyd-Heller 93
              ), it is shown that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thompson%27s+group+F"} Thompson's group F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:G\to G
              its canonical endomorphism, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              does not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} split
              in the quotient of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              by conjugacy. Since the quotient of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              by conjugacy embeds as the full subcategory of the unpointed homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top)
              on connected
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-types"} homotopy 1-types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B g:B G \to B G
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              which does not split in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top)
            %p
              Thus, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:Ho(Top)^{op} \to Set
              splits the idempotent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,B g]
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,B G]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              satisfies the hypotheses of the Brown representability theorem (being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a representable functor), but is not representable. A similar argument using
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G_+
              applies to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top_*)
            %p There is also another example due to Heller, which fails to be representable for cardinality reasons.
            %ul
              %li
                MO questions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/104866/brown-representability-for-non-connected-spaces"} non-connected spaces
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/11456/unpointed-brown-representability-theorem"} unpointed spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2012/08/brown_representability.html"} blog post
          %h2#InInfinity1Categories
            For homotopy functors on presentable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#ClassicalFormulation"} classical formulation
            of Brown representability is only superficially concerned with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            at the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi whe
                  %mi Top
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{whe} Top\simeq
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %p
            We discuss now the natural formulation of the Brown representability theorem for functors out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} homotopy categories of (∞,1)-categories
            following (
            %a{:href => "#LurieHigherAlgebra"}> Lurie, section 1.4.1
            ). See also the exposition in (
            %a{:href => "#Mathew11"}> Mathew 11
            ).
          #BrownFunctorOnInfinityCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \;\colon\; Ho(\mathcal{C})^{op} \longrightarrow Set
            %p
              (from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+functor"} Brown functor
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it sends small
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              %li
                %p
                  it sends
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pushouts"} (∞,1)-pushouts
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}\to Ho(\mathcal{C})
                  to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pullbacks"} weak pullbacks
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          #WeakPullbacks.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+pullback"} weak pullback
              is a diagram that satisfies the existence clause of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BrownFunctorOnInfinityCategory"}
              says that for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pushout"} (∞,1)-pushout
              square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %munder
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mi Z
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Z &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \underset{Z}{\sqcup}Y
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
