          %p
            The generalization of the Brown representability theorem to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-graded
            equivariant cohomology is represented by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+G-spectra"} genuine G-spectra
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#May96"} May 96, chapter XIII.3
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#multiplicative_cohomology_and_ring_spectra Multiplicative cohomology and ring spectra
          %p
            The spectrum Brown-representing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            inherits (at least) the structure of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-ring+spectrum"} H-ring spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "multiplicative+cohomology+theory#BrownRepresentabilityByRingSpectra"} there
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exact+functor+theorem"} Landweber exact functor theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p The original version of the theorem:
          %ul
            %li#Brown62
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cohomology theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1970209"} jstor:1970209
          %p The category-theoretic generalization:
          %ul
            %li#Brown65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1965-0182970-6"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1965-0182970-6
          %p A simplified version of the proof was spelled out in
          %ul
            %li#Spanier66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Spanier"}> Edwin Spanier
              , section 7.7 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology
          %p and a strengthening in
          %ul
            %li#Adams71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Frank+Adams"}> John Frank Adams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A variant of E. H. Brown’s representability theorem
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , part III, section 6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
            %li#Switzer75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Switzer"}> Robert Switzer
                , theorem 8.42, theorem 9.27 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology - Homotopy and Homology
            %li#Kochmann96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochmann"}> Stanley Kochmann
                , section 3.4 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
            %li#AguilarGitlerPrito02
              %p
                Marcelo Aguilar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
            %li#TamakiKono06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
          %p Quick reviews include
          %ul
            %li#Muro10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Muro"}> Fernando Muro
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Representability of cohomology theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://personal.us.es/fmuro/praha.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lurie
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em Phantom maps
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture17.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Neeman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Neeman"}> Amnon Neeman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Grothendieck duality theorem via Bousfield’s techniques and Brown representability
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/jams/1996-9-01/S0894-0347-96-00174-9/"} AMS
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            version, with applications to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            – or rather to the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} models for ∞-stack (∞,1)-toposes
            in terms of the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            – is given in
          %ul
            %li#Jardine09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"}> Rick Jardine
              ,
              %em Representability theorems for simplicial
              %p
                presheaves_, 2009 (
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/JardineBrownrep.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            A version in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#LurieHigherAlgebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 1.4.1 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p Exposition of this is in
          %ul
            %li#Mathew11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://amathew.wordpress.com/2011/10/10/brown-representability-and-infinity-categories/#more-2907"} Brown representability and infinity-categories
          %p
            The case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            theory is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#May96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              , chapter XIII.3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant homotopy and cohomology theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/alaska.pdf"} pdf
          %p The counterexamples to nonconnected and unpointed Brown representability are from
          %ul
            %li#FreydHeller93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Heller"} Alex Heller
              %em Splitting homotopy idempotents. II.
              J. Pure App#l. Algebra 89 (1993), no. 1-2, 93–106.
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+contexts"} Grothendieck contexts
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"}> six operations
            ) is highlighted in
          %ul
            %li#Neeman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Neeman"}> Amnon Neeman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Grothendieck duality theorem via Bousfield’s techniques and Brown representability
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/jams/1996-9-01/S0894-0347-96-00174-9/"} web
        .revisedby
